            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kona Peaberry"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Crazy good vegan grub. I never would have thought to use pumpkin for tacos. It only needed a little help. I felt that the squash would compliment a touch of the Carribean so I chopped it small and added a can of rinsed black beans for protein, a one inch piece of ginger (minced), a dash of chipolte hot sauce, a pinch of allspice, and a squeeze of lime over it. I just stirred in the topping ingredients and served it with a pile of tortillas, yellow rice, and fruit salad."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Stephen Pearce"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added black beans, a half tablespoon of chili powder and a quarter tablespoon of cayenne. The hot pumpkin base is delicious with the cool avocado and tomato.",
            "datePublished": "2014-11-08T17:49:52.213Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "cowgirll"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These were tasty, easy, and healthy. We wound up needing to sort of par-cook the pumpkin first to make peeling and cubing it easier, but after that it was done in a snap. Would have liked a little more flavor though, and I think next time I'll add some lime juice and maybe jalapenos.",
            "datePublished": "2016-11-05T13:26:04.300Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Caramel0"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Soooo good! although i mostly only borrowed the idea of a pumpkin taco - added garam masala, cinnamon and maple syrup to pumpkin while it simmered in apple juice, added indian spiced chicken with lots of cayenne and sauteed collards with black eyed peas, all rolled up in a soft taco topped with tomatoes and avocado - just like my favorite burrito at Mamacitas in Asheville, NC!",
            "datePublished": "2011-11-29T20:34:45.647Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ROBORG"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I enjoyed this! Given the other reviews I spiced it up a little more with 1 tsp of coriander and ground red pepper, as well as a little cayenne and white pepper. I also used a vegetable bouillon cube dissolved in 1/2 cup hot water rather than stock and added some fake meat crumbles. In some fresh corn tortillas it was delicious, and all the garnishes gave it an interesting blend of vegetable tastes. It was just a little bit bland, I'll probably spice/salt it up more next time. I never would have thought to make something like this. Thanks!",
            "datePublished": "2008-10-22T15:26:29.977Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Leia Spencer"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I followed some suggestions and added black beans and lots more spice (cumin, Tabasco). I used our Halloween jack-o-lantern and mashed it together with the black beans, it was yummy! Much better than TVP that I normally use for taco night.",
            "datePublished": "2011-11-04T14:17:52.510Z"
          },
          {
